{"cases":[{"attack":false,"case":"","target":"133434d829d9f5c89f952dcd74c7e74ca701a5fecf83dcfe101ba90d6f1108a8"},{"attack":true,"case":"The self-refutation condition is internally inconsistent with the named relation. SRC_002 declares a contradiction, but its REFUTED-IF condition attacks the wrong failure mode: it says the relation is refuted if 14ab0ddd3b5e 'explicitly acknowledges the underdetermination as a caveat rather than resolving it.' But acknowledging a tension and then resolving it is still a contradiction (the two positions are opposed even if the artifact notes it); it is not the same as the two being 'compatible.' The actual refutation for a contradiction would be if 14ab0ddd3b5e ALSO treated the linear model as empirically assumed (not domain-entailed), making the two compatible/aligned. By framing refutation as mere acknowledgement + caveat rather than actual co-existence, the clause cannot reliably distinguish a surviving contradiction from a dissolved one, leaving the proposed relation logically under-defended.","target":"80cd3d6ff93f4b93ebf4385a72e314658ddd9cb8bdde0f4371cf5ea128a4c819"},{"attack":true,"case":"The dependence claim overstates the semantic requirement. The stated REFUTED IF is that the linear pricing model is self-grounding and needs no contrast with a nonlinear alternative. But routine, domain-default pricing models (uniform unit rate) are epistemically meaningful without adversarial contrast: a solver applies the standard convention unless told otherwise, which is self-grounding in a way that does not require SRC_004's counterfactual. By defining refutation so narrowly (only if 'self-grounding'), the target omits the weaker but sufficient condition that the linear model is simply the default convention, under which there is no dependence on SRC_004. The proposed adversarial dependence is therefore not robust to the default-convention counterexample.","counterexample":["A solver applies uniform-unit pricing by default convention (no nonlinear alternative need be raised), making the linear assumption meaningful without SRC_004."],"target":"c77c4e56ab871f76c5526dde19ae1ef15a889005571d0dfec3b8c9f29427f3e8"}]}